Subject: Sky boxes and cube maps from their .dds, and one side at a time

The map "cave" has a sky of six 2048x2048 PNGs. The engine decoded them twice at load: once as the sky textures (12 MB each, then compressed to DXT1 on the PPE/SPUs), and once more for the sky environment map, where all six sides stayed decoded at once (72 MB) until the upload scaled them to 128x128.

The data ships a 256x256 DXT1 .dds next to each side. The new skydds variable (default 1) makes loadsky and cubemapload use a .dds sibling when there is one; skydds 0 gives the old behaviour. Cube maps built from uncompressed sides are now shrunk to the environment map size as each side loads, so the full-size copies no longer pile up.

